============================================================================================
(C) SMALL-ROOT RESIDUE FORMULA  F(t) = sum_i R(z_i)/(M R(z_i) - z_i R'(z_i))
============================================================================================
  (M,N)=(1,1): residue F = 1.0081956635   series = 1.0081956635   match: True
  (M,N)=(1,2): residue F = 1.0079350054   series = 1.0079350054   match: True
  (M,N)=(2,2): residue F = 0.9924461790   series = 0.9924461790   match: True
  (M,N)=(2,3): residue F = 0.9924492711   series = 0.9924492711   match: True

  F(t) is a symmetric function of the M small roots of z^M = t R(z); its algebraic
  degree, and hence the recurrence order, is set by how those M roots sit among the
  D roots -- and the singular t (branch points) are where roots COLLIDE, i.e. where
  the t-discriminant vanishes.  That is the m-recurrence's apparent-singularity
  structure, and (B) shows its m=0 trace is the R-discriminant itself.
